[{:db/id "q-115643/selection/28e04ed5b1cc5c0f03fa24cdd54b5e2650dde4b569abb509f1beebc745750327" :answer/id #uuid "69a0dbc2-368b-50cf-8181-53aaf11d8756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115643/selection/d4c0ac31ee2cc1532440808dab90cb31c3510b2f04738a066b399873d71b4bc7" :answer/id #uuid "36fa5fed-3280-56d5-b4a5-e6d52d91da01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115643/selection/cf0d2184bb8a898d409675a54a038f84112a96564586e8d81178f9fce24c66d4" :answer/id #uuid "a99a99b6-7751-5bd4-87be-086d24316fd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=3(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115643/selection/41d26337d2f8abc266281b10c06ee35ad125a26a422ecf4ff31e9d8e86f0011b" :answer/id #uuid "5cc6ebe0-056c-5db3-aa4d-00da2d08a862" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115643/selection/edea2149d13533fbfd65a8273c87e73d9e4223169de7dedb96475fdf0a89a605" :answer/id #uuid "88381818-e2b1-51c9-9e9e-465ad7fc25b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}=3y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115643/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "07b63f6e-8114-5be1-acc3-057df4a03f76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115643/selection/41d26337d2f8abc266281b10c06ee35ad125a26a422ecf4ff31e9d8e86f0011b" :answer-field/choices ["q-115643/selection/28e04ed5b1cc5c0f03fa24cdd54b5e2650dde4b569abb509f1beebc745750327" "q-115643/selection/d4c0ac31ee2cc1532440808dab90cb31c3510b2f04738a066b399873d71b4bc7" "q-115643/selection/cf0d2184bb8a898d409675a54a038f84112a96564586e8d81178f9fce24c66d4" "q-115643/selection/41d26337d2f8abc266281b10c06ee35ad125a26a422ecf4ff31e9d8e86f0011b" "q-115643/selection/edea2149d13533fbfd65a8273c87e73d9e4223169de7dedb96475fdf0a89a605"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115643" :question/id #uuid "77c89899-e75a-59ab-bd2e-ad4bcdbad022" :question/math-academy-id "q-115643" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068340/assets/1f6330a6e9bc0e48326982c7b7509f3e2257de994c5736c813ede93a07491e70.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,-3)$ and passes through the point $(3,0).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(0,-3),$ we substitute $h=0$ and $k=-3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(3,0),$ so we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=0$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (0+3)^{2} & =4p(3) \\\\ 9 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{3}{4})x \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{3}{4}$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115643/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115643"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115646/selection/c93c7c9422308179e7153685ccee4cef80db1b69993894c740f4c3fcf044fba5" :answer/id #uuid "4d98b6c9-d61a-5361-a763-b6e14255ae15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+3)^{2}=-9(y-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115646/selection/ff73b35f037673d55cb594e24fafe5286cb637ca5c7854207cf308af109c5497" :answer/id #uuid "2e909bea-71d8-5738-acdb-2bbf15181ddd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=\\frac{9}{8}(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115646/selection/305a5d5cb319f7d39066b0b4b88f6e13e426ed8c42d1bd1fb6f4ba459f729b2c" :answer/id #uuid "9efed647-67d0-564d-9911-ad62bb315100" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=36(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115646/selection/24d3bc532170d58175906d28ec54812fccc0676fbfccb140fe11d6cf5c334d73" :answer/id #uuid "42d05c86-a4fd-5d27-a816-2fb3d493a1c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-3)^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115646/selection/73aa1d7f16aa1522c8a24f29c4ea35148b91395a327630c3c8c3b3f8ee1302e8" :answer/id #uuid "384be47f-c0e6-5e19-8751-565d9f5e163e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115646/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e5a7402-d90a-5909-85eb-d6a5f0698f31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115646/selection/73aa1d7f16aa1522c8a24f29c4ea35148b91395a327630c3c8c3b3f8ee1302e8" :answer-field/choices ["q-115646/selection/c93c7c9422308179e7153685ccee4cef80db1b69993894c740f4c3fcf044fba5" "q-115646/selection/ff73b35f037673d55cb594e24fafe5286cb637ca5c7854207cf308af109c5497" "q-115646/selection/305a5d5cb319f7d39066b0b4b88f6e13e426ed8c42d1bd1fb6f4ba459f729b2c" "q-115646/selection/24d3bc532170d58175906d28ec54812fccc0676fbfccb140fe11d6cf5c334d73" "q-115646/selection/73aa1d7f16aa1522c8a24f29c4ea35148b91395a327630c3c8c3b3f8ee1302e8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115646" :question/id #uuid "6abb456a-0967-521f-9352-1d7bccf90856" :question/math-academy-id "q-115646" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(1,-3)$ and passes through the point $(3,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(1,-3),$ we substitute $h=1$ and $k=-3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(3,0),$ so we can substitute $x=3$ and $y=0$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (0+3)^{2} & =4p(3-1) \\\\ 9 & =8p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{8})(x-1) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =\\frac{9}{2}(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115646/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115646"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
